## Third-party components

Qask is distributed with dependencies under their respective licenses. Before
shipping a packaged application, generate and include a complete dependency
notice file for the exact lockfile and target platform.

Shipped inside the packaged macOS app (`Qask.app/Contents/Resources/`):

- `LICENSE` — the AGPL-3.0-or-later text that governs Qask itself
- `NOTICE` — this file
- `PRIVACY.md` — the local-data boundary

The currently resolved direct runtime components include:

- Electron — MIT
- electron-screenshots — MIT

`node-screenshots` — Apache-2.0 — is a transitive runtime dependency of
`electron-screenshots`, not a direct Qask dependency.

Development-only tooling that is not shipped in a packaged app:

- patch-package — MIT (applies `patches/electron-screenshots+0.5.27.patch` at install time)

This notice is not a substitute for the complete notices required in a binary
release. Regenerate the full dependency notice list from the exact lockfile for
each signed build, and verify that the packaged app contains the license files
listed above (see `docs/release-checklist.md`).

